The legal texts are official texts of the Republic of Suriname, published in the Staatsblad van de Republiek
Suriname and read from:

  De Nationale Assemblee, Surinaamse wetten, https://www.dna.sr/wetgeving/surinaamse-wetten/
  Surinaams Rechtsinformatiesysteem, https://sris.sr/
  retrieved 28 October 2026.

Neither site publishes a licence. Their copyright status under Surinamese law is not confirmed here; they are
reproduced as official texts with the attribution above.

Changes made by Lexifina: each version was converted to one Markdown file per provision, one paragraph per line;
spacing, quotes and dashes were normalised; words broken at a line end were joined; footnotes and page furniture were
removed from the text and the footnotes used only to credit the amending law; where two publishers break a paragraph
differently but the words agree, the older text takes the newer line breaks; and the versions were arranged as git
commits credited to the laws that made each change. The wording of the law was not changed. Neither publisher
endorses this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the tools) are
dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
